# Keep Blossom rules isolated and evidence-based

- Applies only to GaryWenneker/blossom, never to AX, Loom or other workspaces.
- Independent, local-first, security-first music-label pilot, NOT a guaranteed autonomous music factory. Treat current code, tests and README as authoritative; older chat claims and PR messages are historical, not deployment proof.
- Before editing, inspect current main and relevant modules; use AX preflight/explore only when AX is actually scoped to the Blossom project.
- Distinguish: requested design, implemented source, CI passed, user Mac verified, Cloudflare reachable, OAuth granted, MCP tools listed, plugin installed, external provider feature tested. Never conflate.
- Never falsely assert saved/deployed/merged/connected or background work without real tool confirmation.
- Never commit personal passwords, auth codes, bearer tokens, cookies, private env, unredacted traces or real user identity data to policy files.
- Preserve user data, consent, and existing settings. Do not silently delete data or reconfigure provider accounts.
